course: dictionary
lesson: 14655
title: Predictable patterns
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Predictable means you can guess what will happen before it happens, because it follows a pattern. «Tides are predictable.» People can work out when the tide will come in, so they can plan a trip to the beach.
explain: Predictable can also mean that something is always the same, so you know what will happen next. «The story had a predictable ending.» You saw the ending coming, so the story may feel a little dull. Predictable can be useful or boring, depending on the situation.
explain: Look for clue words in the context. Words like always, every, pattern and routine often point to something predictable. «Her routine is predictable: breakfast, school, reading, bed.» The day goes the same way every time.
fact: Predictable means able to be guessed or known before it happens.
fact: Predictable patterns let you say what comes next, such as 2, 4, 6, 8, then 10.
fact: In science, tides and the seasons are predictable, so scientists can plan around them.
fact: «Predictable» can also mean always doing the same thing, which is sometimes boring.
fact: Useful phrases include «a predictable pattern», «predictable results» and «utterly predictable».
exercise: «Tides are predictable.» What does predictable mean here? | Always changing with no pattern | *Able to be known before it happens | Very loud and sudden | Hard to see
exercise: «The story had a predictable ending.» What does this suggest? | The ending was a complete surprise | *You could guess the ending | The story had no ending at all | The ending was written in another language
exercise: The pattern 2, 4, 6, 8 is predictable. What comes next? | 7 | 12 | 9 | *10
test: «Her routine is predictable.» What does this tell you about her day? | It is full of surprises | *It goes the same way every day, so you know what happens | It only happens in the morning | It is very short
test: In science, what are predictable results? | Results with no numbers | Results that nobody can read | Results that are wrong | *Results you can guess before the experiment
exam: Is «predictable» the same as «surprising»? | *No, predictable means you can guess what happens, and surprising means you did not expect it | Yes, both mean boring | No, predictable means very loud | Yes, they mean exactly the same
